Spec: Invoice Service

Platform: Python 3

Purpose:
  Create validated invoices and persist them through the repository boundary.

Structure:
  ./service.py: Service implementation.
  ./models.py: Invoice and invoice line models.
  ./repository.py: Persistence boundary.
  ../../tests/test_service.py: Service behavior tests.

Owns:
  ./service.py
  ./service.sdd

Can modify:
  ./service.py
  ./service.sdd

Can read:
  ./models.py
  ./repository.py
  ../../tests/test_service.py
  ../../tests/test_service.sdd

References:
  ./models.py
  ./repository.py
  ../../tests/test_service.py

Must:
  Validate customer id, invoice lines, quantities, and unit prices before saving.
  Create immutable @invoice_demo.models.Invoice values.
  Save each created invoice through @invoice_demo.repository.InvoiceRepository.save.
  Return the saved invoice to the caller.
  Keep persistence details behind the repository.
    This keeps service behavior easy to test with an in-memory repository.

Must not:
  Perform command-line parsing.
  Read or write files.
  Catch validation errors that callers should handle.

Depends on:
  @invoice_demo.models.Invoice
  @invoice_demo.models.InvoiceLine
  @invoice_demo.repository.InvoiceRepository

Raises:
  ValueError when customer_id is blank.
  ValueError when no invoice lines are provided.
  ValueError when quantity or unit price is not positive.

Scenario: valid invoice is saved
  Given a repository and a valid customer id
  And one line item with positive quantity and unit price
  When @invoice_demo.service.InvoiceService.create_invoice is called
  Then the invoice is saved in @invoice_demo.repository.InvoiceRepository
  And the returned invoice total is positive

Scenario: invalid invoice is rejected
  Given a blank customer id or invalid line item
  When @invoice_demo.service.InvoiceService.create_invoice validates the request
  Then ValueError is raised
  But no invoice is saved

Example: valid input
  source: ./service.py
  test: ../../tests/test_service.py
  symbol: @invoice_demo.service.InvoiceService.create_invoice
  line tuple: `("Design work", 2, "125.00")`
